{"w":2400,"h":2857,"lines":[{"h":0.020412757398366455,"c":1,"y":0.054389018809571033,"t":"Reading","w":0.072264811197916723,"x":0.84720003156264279},{"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","y":0.10461861427790176,"h":0.016095171448565426,"w":0.26297576904296871,"x":0.19550173247678557,"c":1},{"h":0.018983839607639164,"w":0.71626296997070305,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","y":0.14380685803335913,"x":0.19550173291795431,"c":1},{"y":0.16270118983293902,"x":0.19550172727000767,"w":0.14532872517903647,"t":"Passage 2 below.","c":1,"h":0.016095171448565426},{"t":"How could multilingualism benefit India's poorest","y":0.1980322410848171,"w":0.69749842325846356,"h":0.033554051788308725,"c":1,"x":0.20921121339587273},{"x":0.44636678209508424,"w":0.21972318013509112,"c":1,"y":0.23255813892983901,"h":0.023255814698461497,"t":"schoolchildren?"},{"c":1,"w":0.69550170898437491,"h":0.01904486809017103,"t":"The crowded and bustling streets of Delhi teem with life. Stop to listen and, above the din","x":0.19550174056494038,"y":0.27746675978307345},{"y":0.29636109190291304,"w":0.71799306233723947,"h":0.017592396746155647,"x":0.19550173863206283,"c":1,"t":"of rickshaws and buses, you'll hear a multitude of languages, as more than 20 million people"},{"y":0.31276875492987888,"w":0.69039433797200522,"t":"go about their daily lives. Many were born and raised here, and many millions more have","x":0.1937430107726171,"h":0.02053094694379165,"c":1},{"w":0.709342549641927,"c":1,"x":0.1937716316642685,"t":"recently made India's capital their home, having moved from surrounding neighbourhoods,","h":0.018994011021394419,"y":0.33275017499085213},{"y":0.3502449266743658,"w":0.70242212931315118,"x":0.19377163420092292,"t":"cities and states or across the country, often in the hope of gaining better jobs and a better","h":0.018941119803341233,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.68348714192708337,"y":0.36908784884054358,"t":"life. Some arrive speaking fluent Hindi, the dominant language in Delhi (and the official","h":0.01986953075988207,"x":0.19371765456980777},{"y":0.38803358988935566,"c":1,"t":"language of government), but many arrive speaking any number of India's 22 officially","h":0.017494751574527623,"w":0.67474049886067711,"x":0.19204151517444737},{"x":0.19377162788379318,"w":0.68512110392252601,"t":"recognised languages, let alone the hundreds of regional languages in a country of more","y":0.40692792165198099,"c":1,"h":0.017494751574527623},{"t":"than 1.3 billion people.","w":0.18056868235270185,"h":0.019551746323026808,"x":0.19345668584911413,"y":0.42318546727135065,"c":1},{"y":0.46053897575031388,"t":"A team of researchers led by Professor Ianthi Tsimpli of Cambridge University is currently","w":0.70771952311197928,"h":0.018978345802899699,"x":0.19371876751674666,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.71626296997070316,"t":"working on a project collecting data on 1,000 primary-age children in Delhi and the cities of","x":0.19377162909963375,"y":0.47965116281879494,"h":0.018949257067819802},{"y":0.4985465116561274,"c":1,"x":0.19377161448879576,"t":"Hyderabad and Bihar. The overriding aim of the four-year project, called 'Multilingualism","w":0.70415227254231771,"h":0.018948239993181404},{"h":0.020454618962516768,"c":1,"w":0.674740447998047,"y":0.5145348838588879,"x":0.19204153669301821,"t":"and Multiliteracy', is to find out why in a country where multilingualism is so common"},{"t":"(more than 255 million people in India speak at least two languages, and nearly 90 million","c":1,"h":0.017600534010634217,"y":0.53488372064859047,"w":0.69896194458007821,"x":0.19204151896864527},{"w":0.68339101155598958,"h":0.017599516935995929,"y":0.55377906948456046,"c":1,"x":0.19204151832032815,"t":"speak three or more languages), the many benefits of speaking more than one language,"},{"h":0.019051987612639487,"t":"observed in schools in Europe for instance, do not apply to many of India's schoolchildren.","x":0.1937716316487833,"y":0.57122093026072707,"w":0.70934254964192711,"c":1},{"h":0.019035713751054173,"y":0.6074177745874989,"t":"'Each year across India, 600,000 children are tested, and year after year over 50% of children","w":0.72145329793294266,"x":0.19204151702806371,"c":1},{"y":0.62496902246344832,"x":0.1902401073340034,"h":0.020895279229646624,"c":1,"t":"in Standard 5 [ten-year-olds] cannot read a Standard 2 [seven-year-olds] task fluently, and","w":0.69737197875976564},{"t":"just under 50% of them cannot solve a Standard 2 subtraction task, says Tsimpli. She","h":0.018983839607639164,"y":0.64380685803299242,"c":1,"x":0.19031142536387183,"w":0.67128026326497403},{"t":"explains that low educational achievement can lead to many of these students dropping out","y":0.66046607530729728,"w":0.71123224894205728,"h":0.021404902362756828,"x":0.19196848732097957,"c":1},{"w":0.52076126098632813,"c":1,"y":0.6815955212472925,"t":"of school - a problem disproportionately affecting female students.","h":0.017532386005633782,"x":0.19204151474431475},{"x":0.192041526604984,"y":0.71798460469336578,"h":0.017494751574527623,"c":1,"t":"Tsimpli and her colleagues are investigating whether these low learning outcomes could","w":0.67820068359375008},{"t":"be caused by an Indian school system where the language that children are taught in often","w":0.6989619445800781,"y":0.73687893645655633,"x":0.19204151897006055,"c":1,"h":0.017494751574527623},{"h":0.020517299857650162,"c":1,"y":0.75356980345131286,"t":"differs from the language used at home. The research project, which focuses on 8 to 11-year-","w":0.7146632385253906,"x":0.19196585581828118},{"h":0.0175069578049315,"w":0.7128027852376303,"x":0.19204151386108179,"y":0.77325581367175356,"c":1,"t":"old schoolchildren in rural and urban areas, collects data on whether the schoolchildren live"},{"c":1,"y":0.79051934761831666,"t":"in slum* or non-slum areas. Many of the children have moved from remote, rural areas to","x":0.19024781462109475,"w":0.69734268188476567,"h":0.020825829849616784},{"c":1,"t":"urban areas. They are so poor they have to live in slums and, as a result of migration, they","x":0.19204151896687885,"y":0.80959302328420824,"w":0.6989619445800781,"h":0.01895841140693677},{"x":0.19204153444931429,"c":1,"y":0.8284883718091397,"h":0.017557814206336286,"w":0.51903111775716149,"t":"may speak languages that are different from the regional language."},{"x":0.19204152159198495,"y":0.93456962901614027,"w":0.62283737182617183,"c":1,"h":0.0116513014006564,"t":"* slum: a very densely populated area in which the infrastructure is incomplete and services inadequate or non-existent"},{"h":0.014534884186538477,"x":0.88927335676311681,"y":0.95784883691043055,"c":1,"t":"85","w":0.022491348584492976}]}